00:36:16,696 --> 00:36:21,896
なに？ 君は誰？ 私の名前は… 君は名前など…
"What? Who are you?" — "My name is..." — "You have no name..."

334
00:36:22,396 --> 00:36:27,336
そういうあなたわ誰なの？
"Then who on earth are you?"

335
00:36:29,036 --> 00:36:33,216
Who am I? 問いかけてみよう 何故？
Who am I? Let me ask myself, why?

336
00:36:34,456 --> 00:36:38,856
Who am I? 分からないんだ
Who am I? I don't really know.

337
00:36:41,856 --> 00:36:46,496
Who are you? ねえ教えてよ
Who are you? Hey, tell me.

338
00:36:48,076 --> 00:36:52,796
Who am I? 曖昧さ
Who am I? Such ambiguity.

339
00:36:54,456 --> 00:37:04,356
誰か分かってるのは 歌ってる僕は 最後にハッピーってこと
Whoever knows, the me who sings is ultimately happy!

340
00:37:06,996 --> 00:37:13,256
You love music 歌を唄えば 少しずつ見えてくる
You love music. As I sing songs, it slowly comes into view.

341
00:37:14,156 --> 00:37:19,516
僕が生きる意味は きっとここにある
The meaning of my life must be right here.

342
00:37:20,196 --> 00:37:28,456
だってそうぼくは そうねきっと私も 最高なsingerなのさ
Because that's me—that's right, I'm sure I'm the ultimate singer too!

343
00:37:29,676 --> 00:37:36,556
この風変わりなリズムはどこから聴こえてくるのかしら
Where could this eccentric rhythm be coming from, I wonder?

344
00:37:37,056 --> 00:37:40,456
そりゃ私よ 私んことだろ？
Well, that's me! You mean me, right?

345
00:38:01,426 --> 00:38:07,506
それは私だよ 私太っ腹ろ さっかくけったら始めるぞ
"That's me! I'm generous, so once we get set, we're starting!"

346
00:38:07,946 --> 00:38:13,786
お茶はいかが？ お茶はいかが？ 楽しく飲めば 世界も踊る
"How about some tea? How about some tea? If you drink happily, even the world dances!"

347
00:38:14,586 --> 00:38:20,306
お茶はいかが？ さあお茶をどうぞ なんだなんて変なプレイバー
"How about some tea? Now, please have some tea." — "My, what a strange player."

348
00:38:24,546 --> 00:38:29,986
ふだんの味になれちまったら すべてがたいがいに なっちまうもろさ
"If you get too used to ordinary flavors, everything becomes frail and fades away."

349
00:38:30,586 --> 00:38:36,386
ありきたりなものじゃつまらない それを知ったヤツらは みんなイカれちまうのさ
"Ordinary things are boring; those who learn that all go crazy."

350
00:38:37,226 --> 00:38:41,926
ありがたりの ものじゃつまらない
"Things that are taken for granted are boring..."

351
00:38:42,586 --> 00:38:49,246
それを知りたい奴は みんなイカれちまうのさ
"...and those who want to know all go crazy."

352
00:38:50,586 --> 00:38:59,506
ほらお茶はいかが？ きゅうていらいたけりゃ いかれちまえ お茶はいかが？ さあお茶をどうぞ
"Come on, how about some tea? If you want to stay courtly, go crazy! How about some tea? Now, have some tea."

353
00:39:00,726 --> 00:39:03,346
さあ イカれる楽しいディタイム
"Now, a wonderfully crazy teatime!"

354
00:39:26,626 --> 00:39:36,366
迷い込んだ 森の中 私を誘う声が 深い霧にこだまする 私の道はどっち
Wandering deep into the forest, a voice inviting me echoes through the thick fog. Which way is my path?

355
00:39:36,766 --> 00:39:40,046
あっち、そっち、それともこっち
"Over there, that way, or perhaps this way?"

356
00:39:40,146 --> 00:39:49,586
ゆうじゅうふだんな お嬢さん だけどそれは私もう同じ あっちもそっちも歩く道
"Indecisive young lady!" — "But that's the same for me, both paths lead on."

357
00:39:50,606 --> 00:39:55,826
あなあ 喜びや 悲しみや 愛しさまで 詠にしたい 今も全部
Ah, joy, sadness, and even affection—I want to weave them all into song, even now.

358
00:40:00,214 --> 00:40:02,914
繰りかえされていたら
As it was repeated over and over,

359
00:40:03,414 --> 00:40:09,864
最初に見つけていたものが 何か分からなくなって
I forgot what it was I first discovered.

360
00:40:10,214 --> 00:40:19,864
最後に残されたものは 透明な退屈を知らない音楽が
And what was left at the end was music that knows no boredom.

361
00:40:20,264 --> 00:40:29,264
光星の残骸 それを芸術と呼べるのか
The debris of starlight, can that be called art?

362
00:40:30,064 --> 00:40:36,564
頭の中はグチャグチャでも 透明なのは悪くない
My head is a mess, but being transparent isn't bad.

363
00:40:37,064 --> 00:40:44,564
だけど決めた 私は決めた 私の道
Still, I decided, I chose my own path.

364
00:40:50,264 --> 00:40:56,064
幸か不幸か 彼女が選んだ
For better or worse, the path she chose

365
00:40:57,064 --> 00:41:03,564
道は女王へ続く道
leads to the Queen.

366
00:41:06,064 --> 00:41:10,564
女王陛下の おなりー！
Her Majesty the Queen arrives!

367
00:41:21,064 --> 00:41:25,064
私 が女王様さ！
I am the Queen!

368
00:41:25,564 --> 00:41:29,564
何か文句あるのか？
Got a problem with that?

369
00:41:30,064 --> 00:41:34,064
美しい歌声 当たり前じゃない？
Isn't a beautiful singing voice obvious?

370
00:41:34,264 --> 00:41:38,064
オーケストラさあ 始めましょう
Orchestra, let's begin!

371
00:41:38,564 --> 00:41:42,564
あなたが女王様 そうよ覚えておき
You're the Queen? Remember that well.

372
00:41:43,064 --> 00:41:46,864
美しい歌声 当たり前じゃない
A beautiful singing voice is only natural.

373
00:41:47,564 --> 00:41:51,564
オーケストラさあ 始めましょう
Orchestra, now let's begin!

374
00:41:52,064 --> 00:41:55,564
私のミュージック
My music!

375
00:41:56,064 --> 00:41:57,564
ピアノ
Piano!

376
00:41:57,664 --> 00:41:59,064
ウッドベース
Wood bass!

377
00:41:59,264 --> 00:42:00,564
ドラムス
Drums!

378
00:42:00,864 --> 00:42:02,064
ブラスセクション
Brass section!

379
00:42:02,564 --> 00:42:09,064
みんな言うことをお聞き 私のために奏でなさい
Everyone listen to what I say, play for my sake!

380
00:42:09,564 --> 00:42:14,564
すべて私のものよ 私は女王様だからさ
Everything is mine, because I am the Queen!

381
00:42:15,064 --> 00:42:19,064
ちょっと待って！
Wait just a minute!

382
00:42:19,564 --> 00:42:24,564
これはみんなで奏でるミュージック
This is music played together by everyone!

383
00:42:25,064 --> 00:42:29,564
へんてこでもまとまらなくても
Even if it's wacky or uncoordinated,

384
00:42:29,864 --> 00:42:33,564
どんなときでもハッピーを感じてるのさ
we feel happy no matter what time it is.

385
00:42:34,064 --> 00:42:40,064
十人十色だけど 重なればハーモニーになる
Everyone is different, but when combined, it becomes harmony.

386
00:42:41,064 --> 00:42:46,564
理由は単純さ だってwe love music!
The reason is simple, because we love music!

387
00:42:47,064 --> 00:43:03,564
お話をしよう 昔話よりもっともっと素敵な おとぎ話
Let's tell a story, a fairy tale far more wonderful than old tales.

388
00:43:04,064 --> 00:43:12,564
それはありふれた魔法のフィロソフィー みんなのハートに隠されたミュージックランド
It's a common magical philosophy, a music land hidden in everyone's heart.

389
00:43:20,064 --> 00:43:23,064
ミュージック
Music!

390
00:43:53,564 --> 00:43:56,564
Alice in musicland
How do you get to music land?

391
00:44:00,064 --> 00:44:06,064
Over the hill or underland? Or just behind the tree?

392
00:44:07,064 --> 00:44:13,064
When clouds go rolling by, they roll away and leave the sky.

393
00:44:14,064 --> 00:44:19,064
Where is the land beyond the eye that people cannot see?

394
00:44:20,064 --> 00:44:25,064
Where do stars go? Where is the silver crescent moon?

395
00:44:26,064 --> 00:44:32,064
They must be somewhere in the sunny afternoon.

396
00:44:33,064 --> 00:44:39,064
Alice in musicland, where is the path to music land?

397
00:44:40,064 --> 00:44:45,064
Over the hill or here or there? I really wonder where.

398
00:44:46,064 --> 00:44:50,064
Now we know the answer...

399
00:44:50,564 --> 00:44:58,564
When we're enjoying music, always we're in music land!

400
00:45:09,592 --> 00:45:10,592
Yay!

401
00:45:13,672 --> 00:45:15,572
Gimana? Gimana? Gimana?
How was it? How was it?

402
00:45:16,672 --> 00:45:18,172
どうでしたか？
How was it?

403
00:45:21,172 --> 00:45:26,272
Oh, I can't believe it's almost ending, almost, because it still hasn't ended, right?
Oh, I can't believe it's almost ending... because it still hasn't ended, right?

404
00:45:27,172 --> 00:45:35,872
How are you guys enjoying it so far? Are you watching it with popcorn? Are you watching it with something else? With coffee?
How are you guys enjoying it so far? Are you watching with popcorn, or something else? With coffee?

405
00:45:37,072 --> 00:45:48,372
Thank you everyone for coming to my birthday party, because, ah, I am so excited, I'm so happy that my, that my vision is coming to reality.
Thank you everyone for coming to my birthday party, because I am so excited... I'm so happy my vision is coming to reality.

406
00:45:49,072 --> 00:45:53,072
Ah, man, that was really nice, huh? That was really nice.

407
00:45:53,872 --> 00:46:05,172
I hope you guys notice my love for all things like retro, vintage, and like jazz, you know? Always like to create something like a little bit different, like slightly old-school.
I hope you guys notice my love for retro, vintage, and jazz, you know? We always like to create something a little different, slightly old-school.

408
00:46:11,172 --> 00:46:15,072
Makasih semuanya yang udah bikin impian aku jadi realita pokoknya.
Thank you everyone for making my dream a reality, really.

409
00:46:15,572 --> 00:46:20,172
Ah, senang banget, eh, pecah... pecah, curi-curi sikit.
Ah, so happy, ah, epic... epic, stealing a little bit.

410
00:46:21,172 --> 00:46:34,572
Arigatou! Thank you to everyone and my guests that made this happen, amazing special guest, and I am happy if you guys just had fun, groove to the music and stuff.
Arigatou! Thank you to everyone and my guests that made this happen, amazing special guests, and I hope you guys had fun grooving to the music.

411
00:46:35,072 --> 00:46:43,072
So, yeah, I hope you guys enjoyed watching it and thank you for always supporting me! With sticker! Arigatou!
So, yeah, I hope you guys enjoyed watching and thank you for always supporting me! With a sticker, arigatou!

412
00:46:44,072 --> 00:46:47,572
Bye-bye!

413
00:48:26,072 --> 00:48:35,072
This will be a moment I will never forget!!

414
00:48:35,572 --> 00:48:44,572
Thank you for all the support & amazing memories!

